WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.600
In under a week, GPT-6 Astra designed OpenAI's prototype device for hardware teams. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 224. Long context agent memory, radiology report checks, and things to try follow. OpenAI in a progress report on OpenAI.com, laid out workflows for mechanical design, electrical engineering, and simulation that generate editable computer-aided design or CAD models.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.540
printed circuit board layouts and simulation setups from natural language prompts.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.340
The stack output the enclosure, the circuit board, the interface, and the software for

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:44.040
a side project device, though manufacturing still went through human review cycles.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:50.440
The lab is turning 3D scans into editable CAD models for chip-ganassie racing and running

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.740
vehicle design simulations with Mazda.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.100
The work is aimed at engineers who need faster iteration on physical products rather than

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:03.200
pure software tasks, and partners are asked to flag remaining mistakes so later training

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.700
loops can close those gaps.

00:01:05.792 --> 00:01:11.492
Memento, an 8 billion parameter Quinn 3 based agent described on Archive, is trained

00:01:11.492 --> 00:01:16.272
first on synthetic hindsight notes, and then with reinforcement learning that rewards answer

00:01:16.272 --> 00:01:19.112
correctness, note quality, and calibration.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:25.752
It rolls history down into a new 20,000 token window, and at test time also supports folding

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.652
and backtracking.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:32.812
On book-level question answering with inputs up to 2.5 million tokens, it lifts base

00:01:32.812 --> 00:01:43.692
QN38B accuracy from 36.9% to 67.8%, beating a GPT 5.5 agent at 13.1%, at less than

00:01:43.692 --> 00:01:50.812
150th the cost and nearly matching a 100 times larger GLM 5.3 agent at 1.9th the cost.

00:01:50.812 --> 00:01:57.160
SACAM Infant Video is where Gavagai adds an explicit word to region assignment step,

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:02.420
solved with entropic optimal transport plus a nothing column and capacity constraints.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:11.140
The alignment loss raises word-to-picture accuracy from 32.4% to 48.7%, and localization

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:19.400
intersection over union or IOU from 0.18 to 0.38 when added to a next token captioning objective,

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:27.080
and the method is meant for captioning models under high non-reference rates rather than as a replacement for contrastive pre-training.

00:02:27.898 --> 00:02:34.238
Hidden state change from source questions is measured for how much of it transfers to a target question about the same entity

00:02:34.238 --> 00:02:40.878
when injected at 50% depth in work on cross-prompt reuse of entity replacement responses.

00:02:40.878 --> 00:02:48.958
On 0.5 to 1 billion quen and Lama models, other relation hidden reuse removes 45 to 49%

00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:53.838
of no-change error, and a later protocol that restores the beginning of sequence or

00:02:53.838 --> 00:03:00.898
BOS token reaches 58 to 68% on three cohorts, though larger models and chat formats show

00:03:00.898 --> 00:03:02.058
replication failures.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:08.060
Circuit Oracle wraps an off-the-shelf large language model with a multi-agent harness

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:12.960
that answers natural language questions about a target model by reading its attribution

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.260
graph through tool calls.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:20.840
On Spurious Feature Detection, it reaches 78.2% accuracy, outperforming single layer

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:21.800
ranking baselines.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.820
On refusal suppression, its single committed intervention sits slightly below a difference

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:32.620
in means baseline, unless five attempts are allowed, and the authors release pruned subgraphs

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.440
and context-specific feature readings.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:39.878
A production award travel agent found that feeding full record sets into the planner's

00:03:39.878 --> 00:03:47.218
context called synthesis scores 45.7% fully correct turns while keeping records in session

00:03:47.218 --> 00:03:54.198
state and delivering rows over a typed side channel called bypass scores 92.3%.

00:03:54.198 --> 00:04:00.458
Synthesis collapses once tables exceed roughly 74 rows while bypass stays flat across four

00:04:00.458 --> 00:04:06.358
models, and beyond 100 rows, each correct synthesis answer costs roughly 200 times more

00:04:06.358 --> 00:04:12.550
than bypass. ResMEM trains a parametric memory on teacher targets generated by a large

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:18.350
language model that reads retrieved evidence offline, learning an additive-logit residual

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:24.870
rather than mimicking a retriever. On five-question-answering datasets, it raises mean token F1 from

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:33.310
from 32.83% to 34.48%, while breaking 21% fewer of the base models correct answers than

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:39.250
a K nearest neighbors, or KNN, trained memory, and storage for teacher construction drops

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:43.830
94.7% versus the evaluated KNN pipeline.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:50.844
Commercial text humanizers on an October 2026 public leaderboard all altered or dropped

00:04:50.844 --> 00:04:58.464
at least one checkable unit. Numbers, dates, names, quoted spans, in 35 to 65% of documents

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:04.884
containing them. An open 12 billion parameter humanizer retained 97% of numbers and names

00:05:04.884 --> 00:05:12.664
on federal text, but still rewarded 67 to 78% of quoted spans. And a zero-shot decision model,

00:05:12.664 --> 00:05:18.304
Jeff, separated human originals from humanized rewrites at an area under the Curve Score,

00:05:19.144 --> 00:05:21.404
AUROC of 0.864.

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:28.247
Czech's POT decomposes vision-language model radiology reports into rad-graph predicates,

00:05:28.787 --> 00:05:35.887
grounds them against a dense net 121 plus grad-cam table, runs verification code, and rewrites the

00:05:35.887 --> 00:05:38.307
report after dropping unsupported predicates.

00:05:38.307 --> 00:05:48.027
On a 4,145 image held out split, it lifts micro average precision from 19.2% to 46.8%,

00:05:48.027 --> 00:05:57.267
and F1 from 23.0% to 49.4%, for MedGema4B, with similar absolute gains on LLAVA

00:05:57.267 --> 00:05:58.807
Med and Myra2.

00:05:59.989 --> 00:06:04.869
Longitudinal clinical records are what Halo reads as it jointly learns which evidence to keep

00:06:04.869 --> 00:06:10.009
and which patients deserve higher fidelity labels under a fixed budget. In a

00:06:10.009 --> 00:06:14.969
heart failure case study it posted the highest metal line acquired label F1 at

00:06:14.969 --> 00:06:19.369
six of eight target budgets and a downstream classifier trained on halo

00:06:19.369 --> 00:06:26.299
labels reached the highest external MGB F1 at budgets 15 to 60. China's A

00:06:26.299 --> 00:06:31.939
share market is the setting for Astock Arena which audits 3,198 sequential

00:06:31.939 --> 00:06:37.759
trading decisions by 13 models with 8 checks for execution traceability, evidence

00:06:37.759 --> 00:06:45.299
sufficiency, and financial meta-awareness. 72.99% of 1,070 trading points showed at

00:06:45.299 --> 00:06:50.379
least one audit gap, and historical replay confirmed that portfolio outcomes are

00:06:50.379 --> 00:06:57.698
sensitive to the flag trades. Dual-Axis policy entailment or DAPE asks models to

00:06:57.698 --> 00:07:01.038
judge both domain match and the direction of policy change.

00:07:01.618 --> 00:07:03.998
Continue broadened, narrow, reverse.

00:07:04.538 --> 00:07:10.318
On ordered pairs of Chinese government directives, 14 open-weight models and four frontier

00:07:10.318 --> 00:07:16.118
APIs all fall well below human agreement, with the best flagship Kappa at approximately

00:07:16.118 --> 00:07:25.378
0.29 vs 0.53, while a low-rank adaptation or Laura, fine-tuned Quinn 314b reaches the

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:33.700
human ceiling at Kappa of 0.524, said ZodaTagic E5 large, a 560 million parameter in

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:40.340
better, trained on 235,000 synthetic Tagic question passage pairs, plus English and Russian

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:49.340
negatives, raises top 10 recall on unseen law text from 80.2% to 93.6%, and on tax documents

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:53.120
from 82.6% to 94.5%.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:59.360
It matches a 3-billion-parameter model on style-matched law and tax questions, but trails on the

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:01.020
human-written Belebelay set.

00:08:01.961 --> 00:08:08.061
Watermark evidence is stripped under a 20% token-edit budget by a method that uses large language

00:08:08.061 --> 00:08:13.661
model proposed phrase rewrites, an exact coverage search for budgeted KGW evasion.

00:08:13.661 --> 00:08:20.501
39 of 82 initially detected short passages yielded rewrites with Terminal Detector Z below

00:08:20.501 --> 00:08:27.281
4 at a mean 16.0% edit cost, with mean suppression coming mainly from removing watermark and

00:08:27.281 --> 00:08:28.281
rich source events.

00:08:29.255 --> 00:08:34.675
Elsewhere, Sam Altman stated he has long argued for ramping up memory production, and that

00:08:34.675 --> 00:08:36.735
recent remarks were taken out of context.

00:08:37.315 --> 00:08:42.935
A follow-up line from the same open AI CEO said he wants you to have so much RAM, and that

00:08:42.935 --> 00:08:44.295
the industry should build more.

00:08:44.875 --> 00:08:49.195
Control of the future should stay with people rather than be ceded to superintelligence

00:08:49.485 --> 00:08:54.115
in that same set of remarks, and that requirement should constrain AI progress.

00:08:54.835 --> 00:09:00.555
Korean negotiations in an archive study reached agreement 24.8 points more often than

00:09:00.555 --> 00:09:07.335
English ones under identical Gemini 3.6-flash buyer-seller setups, with the gap emerging through

00:09:07.335 --> 00:09:10.355
larger-seller concessions and more politeness mitigation.

00:09:10.355 --> 00:09:16.415
Shift-Rag projects retrieval alignments into continuous soft tokens and adds a soft or

00:09:16.415 --> 00:09:21.735
thogonality objective to mitigate ranked collapse, improving retrieval and question answering

00:09:21.735 --> 00:09:25.915
over state-of-the-art baselines, while preserving backbone capabilities.

00:09:26.475 --> 00:09:33.015
Function calling and math collapse first across 4.1.2 to 1.7 billion instruction-tuned models

00:09:33.015 --> 00:09:38.895
after depth pruning, and uniform healing with a fixed token budget matches or beats planned

00:09:38.895 --> 00:09:45.055
recovery variants on every family. Best-rand reduces high error risk by 50.2%

00:09:45.055 --> 00:09:52.655
and estimation error by 16.4% versus competitive methods, while using only 51.3% of the

00:09:52.655 --> 00:09:59.415
construction cost across 70-plus benchmarks. Decision reliability varies widely on S1 cog bench

00:09:59.415 --> 00:10:06.375
across five open decision models, and Jev on 24 cognitive tasks. Acting well does not imply

00:10:06.375 --> 00:10:11.155
predicting humans, and aggregate scores hide condition-specific response patterns.

00:10:11.715 --> 00:10:19.555
Labidane MedQA collected 39,077 Tetune-translated medical question answer pairs, used to fine-tune

00:10:19.555 --> 00:10:27.475
Gemma and Lama variants, and Gemma 412b with Qlora plus NF4 inference gained 10.79% relative

00:10:27.475 --> 00:10:33.915
accuracy on translated United States medical licensing examination, or USMLE questions.

00:10:33.915 --> 00:10:39.415
sections. Streaming text to SQL failures become reusable dialect instructions offline in

00:10:39.415 --> 00:10:44.535
self-refining prompt induction, and the induced prompt improves mean judge scores across

00:10:44.535 --> 00:10:50.555
seven generators by 7.1 to 19.2 points on held out fling SQL domains.

00:10:51.515 --> 00:10:57.095
QN3's confidence-based early exit gives continuation pieces of a word less computation than the

00:10:57.095 --> 00:11:02.575
first piece in English, German and Turkish, but more in Bangla and resegmenting the same

00:11:02.575 --> 00:11:06.495
Passages with BPE dropout shifts the gap by up to 8 exits.

00:11:07.175 --> 00:11:13.335
Multi-estimate elicitation produced no uniformed biasing across anchoring, hindsight, base

00:11:13.335 --> 00:11:15.935
rate, conjunction, and status quo tasks.

00:11:16.495 --> 00:11:22.375
Six of 23 pre-registered tests rejected after correction, but all fell below pre-specified

00:11:22.375 --> 00:11:23.735
smallest effect sizes.

00:11:24.435 --> 00:11:29.235
MLR adds a high-level planner that emits step descriptors and a low-level executor,

00:11:29.235 --> 00:11:37.435
and iterative step DPO with twisted SMC yields gains of 4.9 points on AIIM25, AIIM26,

00:11:37.855 --> 00:11:44.175
and HMMT26 under a 10% supervised fine-tuning, plus 5% preference budget.

00:11:44.855 --> 00:11:50.575
Electrochemical PDFs yield structured electrolyte, electrode, and property records at an F1

00:11:50.575 --> 00:11:58.655
of 0.97 from Electrochem LLM, which has curated Electrochem DB from 15,000 articles, and

00:11:58.655 --> 00:12:02.795
machine learning models trained on the database support electrolyte property prediction.

00:12:03.415 --> 00:12:06.935
Quantization reshapes a subliminally implanted panda preference.

00:12:07.515 --> 00:12:14.295
4-bit HQQ amplified it while 4-bit NF4 suppressed it despite identical rounding error magnitude.

00:12:14.815 --> 00:12:19.455
And 16-bit audits therefore cannot bound real-world behavior after quantization.

00:12:20.115 --> 00:12:25.595
Switching recorded decisions from deny to approve in near-copy precedence raises approval

00:12:25.595 --> 00:12:31.175
30 to 55 points in three frontier models, while showing the same precedence without decisions,

00:12:31.475 --> 00:12:33.915
but with facts supporting approval, lowers approval.

00:12:34.495 --> 00:12:40.955
Deuce Bench finds content accuracy on jointly grounded tasks reaches at most 56.7%

00:12:40.955 --> 00:12:46.975
across 11 baseline configurations, and matched evidence substitutions show that replacing one

00:12:46.975 --> 00:12:52.155
source's evidence depends on support from the other. Privileged teacher trajectories are projected

00:12:52.155 --> 00:12:55.755
on to actions reachable by the unguided student in SSR.

00:12:56.175 --> 00:12:58.795
On problems with pass at 64 of zero,

00:12:59.035 --> 00:13:02.755
it recovers correct trajectories for 74.6% of cases,

00:13:03.395 --> 00:13:06.395
and yields gains of 4.9 points after fine-tuning

00:13:06.395 --> 00:13:08.375
plus resumed reinforcement learning.

00:13:09.015 --> 00:13:11.995
Adaptive policy distillations per token gate shifts

00:13:11.995 --> 00:13:15.475
roll outs toward the teacher and the objective toward forward KL

00:13:15.475 --> 00:13:19.335
only were needed, improving over plain on-policy distillation

00:13:19.335 --> 00:13:23.655
by up to 54.6% on Casper and Bio-ASQ.

00:13:24.435 --> 00:13:30.315
A formal grammar benchmark shows acceptance rates rising from 16% for GPT 5.5,

00:13:30.655 --> 00:13:37.395
to 52% for GPT 5.5-Pro-X high, with increasing test time compute,

00:13:37.975 --> 00:13:41.575
and responses diverge further from human answers as compute grows.

00:13:42.315 --> 00:13:46.215
Disaster bench nominal tree search reduces to non-adaptive sampling.

00:13:46.215 --> 00:13:51.555
struggling. Structural validation never removes the last correct workflow, yet majority voting

00:13:51.555 --> 00:13:55.635
leaves 10-19% of discovered correct workflows unselected.

00:13:56.535 --> 00:14:02.555
StepDLLM refreshes block sparse masks at anchor steps and uses head-adaptive budgets. On

00:14:02.555 --> 00:14:11.435
LLA Daya 1.5 at 8000 token context and 90% sparsity, it delivers a 2.78 times end-to-end speed-up

00:14:11.435 --> 00:14:15.675
over dense flash attention while improving the accuracy latency trade-off.

00:14:16.155 --> 00:14:22.355
Sentiment sensing combines compositional data analysis, functional data methods, and non-parametric

00:14:22.355 --> 00:14:28.175
inference to enable valid comparisons and detection of shifts across 27 European Union countries

00:14:28.175 --> 00:14:29.915
on energy and AI news.

00:14:30.555 --> 00:14:35.955
Anthropic released flash-proof, which lets developers verify that a response came from a given

00:14:35.955 --> 00:14:41.275
model using cryptographic techniques and is substantially more efficient than prior open-source

00:14:41.275 --> 00:14:47.115
methods, and the code is open-sourced. State bench, on the hugging-face blog, evaluates

00:14:47.115 --> 00:14:50.195
how models track state changes across long documents.

00:14:51.453 --> 00:14:56.713
Try Memento's Compaction Plus reinforcement learning recipe on your own long document

00:14:56.713 --> 00:15:03.433
question-answering tasks. Run checkspots' predicate grounding verification step on any vision-language

00:15:03.433 --> 00:15:09.713
radiology reports you generate. The post-hoc rewrite costs little. Compare Resmem against

00:15:09.713 --> 00:15:14.933
a standard K-nearest neighbor's data store on your retrieval augmented question answering workload

00:15:14.933 --> 00:15:21.353
if you want parametric memory instead of a large store. Test best-rand on any benchmark you

00:15:21.353 --> 00:15:28.045
currently evaluate at full size. OpenAI continues to solicit engineering partners for physical world

00:15:28.045 --> 00:15:33.885
tooling with more CAD, printed circuit board, and simulation primitives expected in the coming weeks.

00:15:34.645 --> 00:15:39.265
Andthropic's open-sourced flash-proof code is set up for community ports to additional

00:15:39.265 --> 00:15:43.445
model families and integration into safety evaluation harnesses.

00:15:44.005 --> 00:15:49.365
Code and model weights are attached to Resmem, Halo, and StepDLLM for early adoption.

00:15:50.267 --> 00:15:56.707
A 200-layer, 3.2-billion-parameter model can outperform a 48-layer 12-billion model on

00:15:56.707 --> 00:16:00.847
multilingual translation when the deeper stack is properly stabilized.

00:16:00.847 --> 00:16:03.767
and that is the gap I want to pop the hood on.

00:16:04.387 --> 00:16:07.207
Transformer layers are sequential transformation blocks.

00:16:07.807 --> 00:16:11.267
Each applies self-attention to mix information across the sequence

00:16:11.597 --> 00:16:15.307
than a feed-forward network that refines every tokens representation

00:16:15.697 --> 00:16:18.787
with residual connections and normalization around both.

00:16:19.487 --> 00:16:23.227
Stacking more layers lets the network build progressively higher level features

00:16:23.227 --> 00:16:24.947
and longer-range dependencies,

00:16:25.267 --> 00:16:27.707
because early layers capture local patterns

00:16:27.707 --> 00:16:30.767
while later layers integrate them into abstract reasoning.

00:16:31.307 --> 00:16:33.787
So depth increases both expressive capacity

00:16:33.787 --> 00:16:37.367
and the amount of sequential computation performed on hidden states.

00:16:38.047 --> 00:16:40.187
The original attention is all you need paper

00:16:40.187 --> 00:16:41.987
showed that this architecture alone,

00:16:42.427 --> 00:16:44.167
without recurrence or convolutions,

00:16:44.887 --> 00:16:47.427
matched or exceeded recurrent models on translation

00:16:47.427 --> 00:16:49.507
while being far more parallelizable.

00:16:50.107 --> 00:16:52.547
Later work on scaling to 1,000 layers

00:16:52.547 --> 00:16:55.647
showed that a modified residual connection called deep norm

00:16:55.647 --> 00:17:01.587
term, plus theoretically derived initialization, keeps updates stable where plain post-layer norm

00:17:01.587 --> 00:17:07.267
or pre-layer norm variance diverge. In practice, the quality gained from added depth diminishes

00:17:07.267 --> 00:17:13.087
once models exceed roughly 70 billion parameters, unless training data and optimization are scaled

00:17:13.087 --> 00:17:18.787
accordingly. When choosing depth versus width, teams should first verify that their optimizer

00:17:18.787 --> 00:17:24.567
and normalization scheme remain stable at the target depth. Otherwise, width scaling or recurrent

00:17:24.567 --> 00:17:27.407
reuse of the same block is often cheaper to stabilize.

00:17:28.582 --> 00:17:33.982
Before we go, depth pruning and quantization audits from more labs are the next write-ups

00:17:33.982 --> 00:17:34.482
to expect.

